t ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•He also that had received two talents came and said, Lord, thou deliveredst unto me two talents: behold, I have gained two other talents beside them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¶His lord said unto him, Well done, good and faithful servant; thou hast been faithful over a few things, I will make thee ruler over many things: enter thou into the joy of thy lord.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ²Then he which had received the one talent came and said, Lord, I knew thee that thou art an hard man, reaping where thou hast not sown, and gathering where thou hast not strawed:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^and I was afraid, and went and hid thy talent in the earth: lo, there thou hast that is thine.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ—His lord answered and said unto him, Thou wicked and slothful servant, thou knewest that I reap where I sowed not, and gather where I have not strawed:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙthou oughtest therefore to have put my money to the exchangers, and then at my coming I should have received mine own with usury.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPTake therefore the talent from him, and give it unto him which hath ten talents.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘For unto every one that hath shall be given, and he shall have abundance: but from him that hath not shall be taken away even that which he hath.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgAnd cast ye the unprofitable servant into outer darkness: there shall be weeping and gnashing of teeth.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse"¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~When the Son of man shall come in his glory, and all the holy angels with him, then shall he sit upon the throne of his glory:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹and before him shall be gathered all nations: and he shall separate them one from another, as a shepherd divideth his sheep from the goats:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHand he shall set the sheep on his right hand, but the goats on the left.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙšThen shall the King say unto them on his right hand, Come, ye blessed of my Father, inherit the kingdom prepared for you from the foundation of the world:¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book'§chapter«first_verse#ªlast_verse(¦verses–„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtfor I was an hungred, and ye gave me meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me drink: I was a stranger, and ye took me in:¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^naked, and ye clothed me: I was sick, and ye visited me: I was in prison, and ye came unto me.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~Then shall the righteous answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, and fed thee? or thirsty, and gave thee drink?¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJWhen saw we thee a stranger, and took thee in? or naked, and clothed thee?¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;Or when saw we thee sick, or in prison, and came unto thee?¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¥And the King shall answer and say unto them, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye have done it unto one of the least of these my brethren, ye have done it  unto me.¦layout ªlast_verse(…¤book'§chapter«first_verse)ªlast_verse-¦verses•„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‹Then shall he say also unto them on the left hand, Depart from me, ye cursed, into everlasting fire, prepared for the devil and his angels:¦layout ªlast_verse)„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUfor I was an hungred, and ye gave me no meat: I was thirsty, and ye gave me no drink:¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrI was a stranger, and ye took me not in: naked, and ye clothed me not: sick, and in prison, and ye visited me not.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§Then shall they also answer him, saying, Lord, when saw we thee an hungred, or athirst, or a stranger, or naked, or sick, or in prison, and did not minister unto thee?¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ†Then shall he answer them, saying, Verily I say unto you, Inasmuch as ye did it not to one of the least of these, ye did it not to me.¦layout ªlast_verse-…¤book'§chapter«first_verse.ªlast_verse.¦verses‘„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYAnd these shall go away into everlasting punishment: but the righteous into life eternal.¦layout ªlast_verse.